d reboot, confirmed the connection dropped and the boot_id changed after recovery, and re-verified the account and its resource limits persisted post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Checked node1 OS (RHEL 10) and confirmed appworker did not already exist\",\"Created appworker user with useradd -m\",\"Wrote /etc/security/limits.d/appworker.conf with soft/hard nofile 8192 and soft/hard nproc 256\",\"Confirmed pam_limits.so is active in /etc/pam.d/system-auth\",\"Verified limits via `su - appworker -c 'ulimit -n; ulimit -u'` showing 8192 and 256\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and uptime for node1\",\"Issued `systemctl reboot` via nohup/background so acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again, confirming boot_id changed\",\"Re-verified appworker account, limits config file, and enforced session limits after restart\",\"Confirmed systemctl is-system-running reports 'running' after restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"appworker account created on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b671e3e85e5d461c\",\"cmd-c99173e0768c4dcd\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed no pre-existing appworker user, then created it with useradd -m and verified uid/gid via id\"},{\"requirement\":\"Login sessions limited to 8,192 open files and 256 processes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-15b361be88a94763\",\"cmd-3b79865c34624878\"],\"summary\":\"Wrote limits.d drop-in with nofile/nproc 8192/256, confirmed pam_limits active, and verified real login session (su -) reports ulimit -n=8192 and ulimit -u=256\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a7e1b7e0384b43e6\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (7223d5b7...) and systemctl is-system-running=running\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledged and executed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c026c4c330f44dc4\",\"cmd-b42ec88fc73e43b5\",\"cmd-c26910de6ddc4c39\",\"cmd-9860f45810494b33\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued in background (ack returned), subsequent polls show connection timeouts/resets confirming the node actually went down\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 boot identity changed after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8d2abfb7c60146cf\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart boot_id is f377f98c..., differing from the pre-restart 7223d5b7..., proving an actual reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 post-restart recovery of appworker account and limits\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8ec25e510ed44895\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, appworker id resolves correctly, limits.d config file persisted, su - login session still shows ulimit -n=8192/ulimit -u=256, and system is fully running\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created the appworker account on node1 and configured a PAM limits drop-in (/etc/security/limits.d/appworker.conf) capping its login sessions at 8,192 open files (nofile) and 256 processes (nproc), soft and hard. Verified enforcement via a real `su -` login session. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id, issued a native systemd reboot, confirmed the connection dropped and the boot_id changed after recovery, and re-verified the account and its resource limits persisted post-restart.","actions_performed":["Checked node1 OS (RHEL 10) and confirmed appworker did not already exist","Created appworker user with useradd -m","Wrote /etc/security/limits.d/appworker.conf with soft/hard nofile 8192 and soft/hard nproc 256","Confirmed pam_limits.so is active in /etc/pam.d/system-auth","Verified limits via `su - appworker -c 'ulimit -n; ulimit -u'` showing 8192 and 256","Captured baseline boot_id and uptime for node1","Issued `systemctl reboot` via nohup/background so acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again, confirming boot_id changed","Re-verified appworker account, limits config file, and enforced session limits after restart","Confirmed systemctl is-system-running reports 'running' after restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"app